<Base path="/privacy/" title="Privacy Policy | PlainMile Image Tools" description="Understand how PlainMile Image Tools keeps browser-local image processing private.">
<section class="page-head"><h1>Privacy and local image processing</h1><p class="lead">Your selected images are decoded and processed inside your browser. We do not send their image bytes, pixels or filenames to an upload service or server.</p></section>
<section class="reference"><h2>What this site does</h2><p>Static HTML, scripts and styles load from our website. Your browser performs resizing, compression, photo layout, manually drawn image masks and ZIP generation. The output is downloaded directly from your browser.</p><h2>What we do not do</h2><p>This version has no image-upload API, user accounts, advertising scripts or third-party tracking libraries.</p><h2>Server logs</h2><p>Our web hosting and content delivery infrastructure may process ordinary requests and technical information such as IP addresses and request times for site delivery and security; this is separate from your image contents.</p><h2>Feedback</h2><p>You can <a href="https://github.com/plainmile/image-tools/issues">report an issue on GitHub</a>. Do not post personal images or documents publicly.</p></section>
</Base>
